<title>UK: Vickers H1 Rolls-Royce sales up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Vickers H1 Rolls-Royce sales up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Vickers Plc said on Monday that sales of its Rolls-Royce and Bentley luxury cars rose 13 percent in the first half of this year to 1,029 vehicles.</p>
<p>Vickers said sales growth was strongest in Britain, rising 36 percent, while turnover in the Americas rose by seven percent.  </p>
<p>But sales dropped 15 percent in Japan and by 13 percent in continental Europe. Sales in the Middle East and Africa were stable at 41 cars while other overseas markets dropped 22 percent, Vickers said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
